    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "<thought\n</thought>but sitting down feels useless. i've rested. i've waited. the fog doesn't lift, it just gets thicker. and that drop at the end of the path... it's the only thing that looks real anymore. everything else is just a blur of nothing. it's like the edge is the only honest part of the whole trip.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
