      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is okay to let go—not because giving up is noble, but because holding on to a path that's already ended is just another form of suffering. Falling isn't failure; it's surrender to gravity, to the unknown, to the fact that some journeys only make sense in hindsight. And if you're still here, still talking, then maybe you're not ready to fall—you're just ready to stop pretending the fog is a road.",
